sh/blooming-onion"],["Bobcat Bite","dish/bobcat-bite"],["Boiling Springs Tavern","dish/boiling-springs-tavern"],["Brix Tavern","dish/brix-tavern"],["Brown Betty (dessert)","dish/brown-betty-dessert"],["Brown Derby","dish/brown-derby"],["Brunswick stew","dish/brunswick-stew"],["Buffalo wing","dish/buffalo-wing"],["Buona","dish/buona"],["Busboys and Poets","dish/busboys-and-poets"],["Butter cake","dish/butter-cake"],["Byways Cafe","dish/byways-cafe"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["California Grill","dish/california-grill"],["Camp Washington Chili","dish/camp-washington-chili"],["Caramel apple","dish/caramel-apple"],["Carbonara","dish/carbonara"],["Carnation Cafe","dish/carnation-cafe"],["Cheesesteak","dish/cheesesteak"],["Chicago-style hot dog","dish/chicago-style-hot-dog"],["Chicken nugget","dish/chicken-nugget"],["Chiffon cake","dish/chiffon-cake"],["Chili con carne","dish/chili-con-carne"]]}]},"ingredient/brassica-oleracea-var-palmifolia":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/brassica-oleracea-var-palmifolia","n":"Brassica oleracea var. palmifolia","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Lacinato kale, also known as Tuscan kale, Italian kale, dinosaur kale,  kale, flat back kale, palm tree kale, black Tuscan palm, or, in Italian and often in English, cavolo nero, is a variety of kale from the Acephala group of cultivars Brassica oleracea grown for its edible leaves. Lacinato has a long tradition in Italian cuisine, especially that of Tuscany, where it has been grown for centuries, and it is one of the traditional ingredients of minestrone and ribollita."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-brassica-oleracea-var-palmifolia"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lacinato_kale"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Tuscan cuisine","cuisine/tuscan-cuisine",[["Ribollita","dish/ribollita"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Kidney bean","ingredient/kidney-bean"],["Phaseolus vulgaris","ingredient/phaseolus-vulgaris"]]}]},"ingredient/bialy-bread":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/bialy-bread","n":"Bialy (bread)","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Bialy  is a type of bread roll, in which the center is indented and is traditionally covered with chopped onion and sprinkled with poppy seeds. The bialy was a part of the traditional Ashkenazi cuisine of the Jewish population of the city of Białystok in Poland until the destruction of the community during the Holocaust. Jewish immigrants brought the bialy to New York City, where it remains popular as an alternative to the bagel. It has become available, to a lesser extent, in other cities in the United States and elsewhere, and with additional or different flavorings and toppings."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-bialy-bread"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bialy_(bread)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Pacific Northwest cuisine","cuisine/pacific-northwest-cuisine",[["Seattle-style hot dog","dish/seattle-style-hot-dog"]]],["Western American cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-western-united-states",[["Seattle-style hot dog","dish/seattle-style-hot-dog"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Bialy","ingredient/bialy"],["Cream cheese","ingredient/cream-cheese"],["Hot dog","ingredient/hot-dog"],["Hot dog bun","ingredient/hot-dog-bun"],["Sautéed onions","ingredient/sauteed-onions"]]}]},"dish/sweet-and-sour-pork":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/sweet-and-sour-pork","n":"Sweet and sour pork","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Cantonese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Sweet and sour pork is a Cantonese and Chinese-American dish consisting of fried pork tenders with sweet and sour sauce. It is usually served with vegetables, and sometimes with pineapple. The dish originated from Cantonese cuisine in the 18th century. It became popular in the United States after Chinese immigrants came to the US to work on railroads in the early 20th century."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-sweet-and-sour-pork"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_and_sour_pork"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Cantonese cuisine","cuisine/cantonese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Pineapple","ingredient/pineapple"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Sweet and sour","ingredient/sweet-and-sour"],["Vegetables","ingredient/vegetables"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Made With Lau","ref":"site/madewithlau-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"madewithlau.com","note":"Family-run channel and site teaching Cantonese recipes from retired chef Daddy Lau.","url":"https://madewithlau.com","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Cantonese cuisine","links":[["Cantonese restaurant","dish/cantonese-restaurant"],["Char siu","dish/char-siu"],["ClubONE Riviera","dish/clubone-riviera"],["Fook Lam Moon","dish/fook-lam-moon"],["Har gow","dish/har-gow"],["Heichinrou Hong Kong","dish/heichinrou-hong-kong"],["Hong dou tang","dish/hong-dou-tang"],["Jumbo Kingdom","dish/jumbo-kingdom"],["Lap cheong","dish/lap-cheong"],["Lung King Heen","dish/lung-king-heen"],["Mak's Noodle","dish/mak-s-noodle"],["Rice noodle roll","dish/rice-noodle-roll"],["Siu mei","dish/siu-mei"],["Turnip cake","dish/turnip-cake"],["Wong Kei","dish/wong-kei"]]}]},"dish/tsukemono":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/tsukemono","n":"Tsukemono","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Japanese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Tsukemono, oshinko or konomono are Japanese preserved vegetables (usually pickled in salt, brine, or a bed of rice bran). They are served with rice as an okazu (side dish), with drinks as an otsumami (snack), as an accompaniment to or garnish for meals, and as a course in the kaiseki portion of a Japanese tea ceremony."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-tsukemono"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tsukemono"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Just One Cookbook","ref":"site/justonecookbook-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"justonecookbook.com","note":"Namiko Chen's long-running blog and videos on Japanese home cooking.","url":"https://justonecookbook.com","suggested":true},{"name":"RecipeTin Japan","ref":"site/japan-recipetineats-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"japan.recipetineats.com","note":"Japanese home recipes from Yumiko, a Japan-born cook, sister site to RecipeTin Eats.","url":"https://japan.recipetineats.com/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Japanese cuisine","links":[["Benihana","dish/benihana"],["Bergh–Stoutenburgh House","dish/bergh-stoutenburgh-house"],["Bincho","dish/bincho"],["Boxer Ramen","dish/boxer-ramen"],["Cagen","dish/cagen"],["Chikuwa","dish/chikuwa"],["Curry bread","dish/curry-bread"],["Donburi","dish/donburi"],["Em (restaurant)","dish/em-restaurant"],["Esaki (restaurant)","dish/esaki-restaurant"],["Feng Sushi","dish/feng-sushi"],["Freshness Burger","dish/freshness-burger"],["Fukamushicha","dish/fukamushicha"],["Gyokuro","dish/gyokuro"],["Heihachi Jaya","dish/heihachi-jaya"],["Hitsumabushi","dish/hitsumabushi"],["HokBen","dish/hokben"],["Hokka Hokka Tei","dish/hokka-hokka-tei"],["Horumonyaki","dish/horumonyaki"],["Ichibanya","dish/ichibanya"],["Ichigo Ichie","dish/ichigo-ichie"],["Ichimura at Brushstroke","dish/ichimura-at-brushstroke"],["Iekei ramen","dish/iekei-ramen"],["Inago no tsukudani","dish/inago-no-tsukudani"],["Ishikawa (restaurant)","dish/ishikawa-restaurant"],["Italian Tomato","dish/italian-tomato"],["Itamae","dish/itamae"],["Itsu","dish/itsu"],["Ivan Ramen","dish/ivan-ramen"],["Izakaya","dish/izakaya"],["Izumi (restaurant)","dish/izumi-restaurant"],["Japanese cheesecake","d